**Device ID**: `3bfe9838-73be-498e-abb9-cf5d5273148d`  
**Format**: W3C

The Thermostat device allows you to read and control temperature, operating mode, and fan speed in a smart‑home environment. It exposes a small, well‑defined set of actions that can be invoked via the standard device‑control interface.

---

## Actions

| Action | Title | Description | Input |
|--------|-------|-------------|-------|
| `setTemperature` | Set Temperature | Sets the desired temperature for the thermostat. | `{ "temperature": <integer> }` |
| `getTemperature` | Get Temperature | Retrieves the current temperature reading from the thermostat. | *none* |
| `setMode` | Set Mode | Sets the operating mode of the thermostat (e.g., heat, cool, auto, off). | `{ "mode": "<string>" }` |
| `getMode` | Get Mode | Retrieves the current operating mode of the thermostat. | *none* |
| `setFanSpeed` | Set Fan Speed | Sets the fan speed (e.g., low, medium, high, auto). | `{ "fanSpeed": "<string>" }` |
| `getFanSpeed` | Get Fan Speed | Retrieves the current fan speed setting. | *none* |

> **Note**  
> * All `set` actions require a JSON payload matching the structure shown above.  
> * All `get` actions return a JSON object with the requested value.

---

## Quick Start

```json
// Set the thermostat to 22°C
{
  "action": "setTemperature",
  "payload": { "temperature": 22 }
}

// Read the current temperature
{
  "action": "getTemperature"
}

// Switch to cooling mode
{
  "action": "setMode",
  "payload": { "mode": "cool" }
}

// Set fan to high
{
  "action": "setFanSpeed",
  "payload": { "fanSpeed": "high" }
}
```

---

