[{'format': 'SmartThings', 'structured': {'name': 'light', 'label': 'Light', 'components': [{'capabilities': [{'id': 'switch', 'commands': {'turn_on': {'arguments': []}, 'turn_off': {'arguments': []}}, 'version': 1, 'status': 'live'}], 'id': 'main', 'label': 'main', 'optional': False}], 'format': 'SmartThings', 'deviceId': 'f9099b6b-f0b1-4003-ad54-f737b137cb63'}}, {'format': 'W3C', 'structured': {'title': 'Garage Door', 'actions': {'close': {'title': 'Close Garage Door', 'description': 'Closes the garage door.'}, 'open': {'title': 'Open Garage Door', 'description': 'Opens the garage door.'}}, 'format': 'W3C', 'id': 'b28f39d0-751d-4db4-843e-b39ebeabef56'}}, {'format': 'W3C', 'structured': {'title': 'Thermostat', 'actions': {'turnOn': {'title': 'Turn On', 'description': 'Turns the thermostat on.'}, 'turnOff': {'title': 'Turn Off', 'description': 'Turns the thermostat off.'}, 'setTemperature': {'title': 'Set Temperature', 'description': 'Sets the target temperature of the thermostat.', 'input': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'temperature': {'type': 'integer'}}, 'required': ['temperature']}}, 'getTemperature': {'title': 'Get Temperature', 'description': 'Gets the current temperature reading from the thermostat.'}, 'setMode': {'title': 'Set Mode', 'description': 'Sets the operating mode of the thermostat (e.g., heat, cool, auto).', 'input': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'mode': {'type': 'string'}}, 'required': ['mode']}}}, 'format': 'W3C', 'id': '92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609'}, 'natural': '# Thermostat

A simple, programmable thermostat that can be turned on/off, set to a target temperature, queried for the current reading, and switched between operating modes (heat, cool, auto).

---

## Features

| Action | Title | Description |
|--------|-------|-------------|
| `turnOn` | Turn On | Turns the thermostat on. |
| `turnOff` | Turn Off | Turns the thermostat off. |
| `setTemperature` | Set Temperature | Sets the target temperature. |
| `getTemperature` | Get Temperature | Retrieves the current temperature reading. |
| `setMode` | Set Mode | Sets the operating mode (e.g., *heat*, *cool*, *auto*). |

---

## API

All actions are invoked by sending a JSON payload that matches the schema below. The device is identified by the ID `92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609`.

```json
{
  "id": "92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609",
  "action": "<action_name>",
  "input": { /* optional, see below */ }
}
```

### Action payloads

| Action | Input Schema | Example |
|--------|--------------|---------|
| `turnOn` | none | `{ "id":"92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609", "action":"turnOn" }` |
| `turnOff` | none | `{ "id":"92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609", "action":"turnOff" }` |
| `setTemperature` | `{ "temperature": integer }` | `{ "id":"92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609", "action":"setTemperature", "input": { "temperature": 72 } }` |
| `getTemperature` | none | `{ "id":"92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609", "action":"getTemperature" }` |
| `setMode` | `{ "mode": string }` | `{ "id":"92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609", "action":"setMode", "input": { "mode": "cool" } }` |

---

## Usage Example (Node.js)

```js
const axios = require('axios');

const deviceId = '92897f59-7fc6-4f84-9a2c-aa3edd073609';

async function turnOn() {
  await axios.post('https://api.smart-home.com/devices', {
    id: deviceId,
    action: 'turnOn'
  });
}

async function setTemp(temp) {
  await axios.post('https://api.smart-home.com/devices', {
    id: deviceId,
    action: 'setTemperature',
    input: { temperature: temp }
  });
}

async function getTemp() {
  const res = await axios.post('https://api.smart-home.com/devices', {
    id: deviceId,
    action: 'getTemperature'
  });
  console.log('Current temp:', res.data.temperature);
}

// Example flow
(async () => {
  await turnOn();
  await setTemp(68);
  await getTemp();
})();
```

