**Device ID:** `a0ffbd24-8cc0-4231-a8cd-c62814ba99ca`  
**Format:** W3C

---

## Overview

The Thermostat device allows you to control and monitor temperature settings in a smart environment. It supports setting a target temperature, querying the current temperature, selecting operating modes (heat, cool, auto, off), and retrieving the current mode.

---

## Actions

| Action | Title | Description | Input | Output |
|--------|-------|-------------|-------|--------|
| `setTemperature` | Set Temperature | Sets the target temperature of the thermostat. | `{ "temperature": <integer> }` | *None* |
| `getTemperature` | Get Temperature | Retrieves the current temperature reading from the thermostat. | *None* | `{ "temperature": <integer> }` |
| `setMode` | Set Mode | Sets the operating mode of the thermostat (e.g., heat, cool, auto, off). | `{ "mode": <string> }` | *None* |
| `getMode` | Get Mode | Retrieves the current operating mode of the thermostat. | *None* | `{ "mode": <string> }` |

---

## Example Usage

```json
// Set target temperature to 72°F
{
  "action": "setTemperature",
  "input": { "temperature": 72 }
}

// Get current temperature
{
  "action": "getTemperature"
}

// Set mode to "cool"
{
  "action": "setMode",
  "input": { "mode": "cool" }
}

// Get current mode
{
  "action": "getMode"
}
```

---

## Notes

- All temperatures are expressed in integer degrees (°F or °C depending on your configuration).
- Modes are case‑sensitive and must match one of the supported strings (`heat`, `cool`, `auto`, `off`).
- The device follows the W3C IoT Device Description format, ensuring interoperability with standard IoT platforms.

