The **TV** device exposes a small set of actions that let you control power, channel, volume and input source.  
All actions are defined in a W3C‑style schema and identified by the UUID `ae354e04-3d0c-4d30-a890-eef1b9461cc0`.

---

## Actions

| Action | Title | Description | Input |
|--------|-------|-------------|-------|
| `turn_on` | Turn On | Power on the TV. | – |
| `turn_off` | Turn Off | Power off the TV. | – |
| `set_channel` | Set Channel | Change the TV channel to a specified number. | `{ "channel": <integer> }` |
| `volume_up` | Volume Up | Increase the TV volume by one step. | – |
| `volume_down` | Volume Down | Decrease the TV volume by one step. | – |
| `mute` | Mute | Mute or unmute the TV sound. | – |
| `set_input` | Set Input | Change the TV input source. | `{ "source": "<string>" }` |

---

## Quick Start

```json
// Turn the TV on
{ "action": "turn_on" }

// Set channel 5
{ "action": "set_channel", "input": { "channel": 5 } }

// Increase volume
{ "action": "volume_up" }

// Mute the TV
{ "action": "mute" }

// Switch to HDMI 2
{ "action": "set_input", "input": { "source": "HDMI2" } }

// Turn the TV off
{ "action": "turn_off" }
```

---

## Notes

- **Channel numbers** are integers; ensure the TV supports the requested channel.
- **Input sources** are case‑sensitive strings (e.g., `"HDMI1"`, `"AV"`, `"TUNER"`).
- The **mute** action toggles the current mute state; repeated calls will alternate between muted and unmuted.

