**Format:** W3C

The Light device provides two simple actions: turning the light on and changing its color.

---

## Actions

| Action | Title | Description | Parameters |
|--------|-------|-------------|------------|
| `turn_on` | Turn On | Turns the light on. | None |
| `set_color` | Set Color | Changes the color of the light. | `color` (string) |

### `set_color` Input Schema

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "color": { "type": "string" }
  },
  "required": ["color"]
}
```

---

## Example Usage

```json
// Turn the light on
{
  "action": "turn_on"
}

// Set the light to blue
{
  "action": "set_color",
  "input": {
    "color": "blue"
  }
}
```

---

### Notes

- The light can only be turned on; there is no `turn_off` action defined in this specification.
- Colors are specified as plain strings (e.g., `"red"`, `"green"`, `"#FF00FF"`).

