## Overview

This SmartThings device represents a single window that can be opened or closed. It exposes a simple `window` capability with two commands: `open` and `close`.

---

## Components

| ID   | Label | Optional | Capabilities |
|------|-------|----------|--------------|
| main | main  | No       | `window`     |

---

## Capabilities

### `window`

| Command | Arguments |
|---------|-----------|
| `open`  | None |
| `close` | None |

---

## Example Usage

### SmartThings Groovy SmartApp

```groovy
definition(
  name: "Window Demo",
  namespace: "example",
  author: "Your Name",
  description: "Demo of the Window device",
  category: "Convenience",
  iconUrl: "",
  iconX2Url: ""
)

preferences {
  section("Select a window") {
    input "win", "capability.window"
  }
}

def openWindow() {
  win.open()
}

def closeWindow() {
  win.close()
}
```

### SmartThings JavaScript (Node.js)

```javascript
const { SmartThingsClient } = require('@smartthings/core-sdk');

const client = new SmartThingsClient({ accessToken: 'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN' });

async function openWindow(deviceId) {
  await client.commands.sendCommand(deviceId, 'open');
}

async function closeWindow(deviceId) {
  await client.commands.sendCommand(deviceId, 'close');
}

openWindow('4ccc9ee1-bc52-4459-ab84-85fc6ecda3a5');
```

---

## Notes

- The device is currently in `live` status and supports the standard SmartThings `window` capability.
- No additional configuration is required beyond adding the device to your SmartThings account.

