**Device ID:** `53d39ebe-fc9d-4d55-a34b-521fe03df3ec`  
**Format:** W3C  

## Overview

This API controls a speaker device. It supports basic playback commands, volume control, muting, input source switching, and status queries. All interactions are performed via JSON payloads that conform to the W3C specification.

## Actions

| Action | Title | Description | Input (if any) |
|--------|-------|-------------|----------------|
| `play` | Play | Play audio | – |
| `pause` | Pause | Pause audio | – |
| `stop` | Stop | Stop audio | – |
| `setVolume` | Set Volume | Set the volume level | ```json{ "level": <integer> }``` |
| `setMute` | Set Mute | Mute or unmute the speaker | ```json{ "state": "<string>" }``` (e.g., `"on"` or `"off"`) |
| `setInputSource` | Set Input Source | Change the input source | ```json{ "source": "<string>" }``` |
| `getStatus` | Get Status | Retrieve the current status of the speaker | – |

## Example Usage

```json
// Play audio
{ "action": "play" }

// Pause audio
{ "action": "pause" }

// Stop audio
{ "action": "stop" }

// Set volume to 75%
{ "action": "setVolume", "payload": { "level": 75 } }

// Mute the speaker
{ "action": "setMute", "payload": { "state": "on" } }

// Unmute the speaker
{ "action": "setMute", "payload": { "state": "off" } }

// Switch to HDMI input
{ "action": "setInputSource", "payload": { "source": "HDMI" } }

// Get current status
{ "action": "getStatus" }
```

## Notes

- All integer values (e.g., `level`) should be within the device‑specific range (typically 0–100).
- The `state` field for `setMute` accepts `"on"` or `"off"`.
- The `source` field for `setInputSource` should match one of the supported input names for the speaker.

