**ID:** `fdaf916c-afc5-4fdf-9893-fa7d3cf0e42e`  
**Format:** W3C

---

## Overview

The Heater device provides basic temperature control capabilities. It can be turned on/off, queried for its current temperature, and set to a desired temperature.

---

## Actions

| Action | Title | Description | Parameters |
|--------|-------|-------------|------------|
| `turnOn` | Turn On Heater | Turns on the heater. | None |
| `turnOff` | Turn Off Heater | Turns off the heater. | None |
| `setTemperature` | Set Temperature | Sets the desired temperature for the heater. | `temperature` (integer) |
| `getTemperature` | Get Temperature | Retrieves the current temperature from the heater. | None |

---

## Example Usage

```json
// Turn the heater on
{
  "action": "turnOn"
}

// Set temperature to 22°C
{
  "action": "setTemperature",
  "input": {
    "temperature": 22
  }
}

// Get current temperature
{
  "action": "getTemperature"
}

// Turn the heater off
{
  "action": "turnOff"
}
```

---

## Notes

- The `setTemperature` action requires an integer value for `temperature`.  
- All actions are synchronous; responses will be returned immediately.  
- The heater’s current temperature can be queried at any time using `getTemperature`.

