A SmartThings‑compatible thermostat that can be controlled via a simple, well‑documented API.

---

## Device Overview

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Name** | thermostat |
| **Label** | Thermostat |
| **Device ID** | `35a42f88-432f-41ea-8b7c-09296637472a` |
| **Format** | SmartThings |
| **Component** | `main` (required) |
| **Capabilities** | `thermostat_control` |
| **Status** | live |

---

## Available Commands

| Command | Arguments | Description |
|---------|-----------|-------------|
| `set_temperature` | `temperature` (integer, required) | Set the target temperature. |
| `get_temperature` | – | Retrieve the current temperature. |
| `turn_on` | – | Power on the thermostat. |
| `turn_off` | – | Power off the thermostat. |
| `set_mode` | `mode` (string, required) | Set the operating mode (e.g., `"heat"`, `"cool"`, `"auto"`). |

### Example Calls

```json
// Turn the thermostat on
{
  "command": "turn_on",
  "arguments": {}
}

// Set temperature to 22°C
{
  "command": "set_temperature",
  "arguments": {
    "temperature": 22
  }
}

// Change mode to "cool"
{
  "command": "set_mode",
  "arguments": {
    "mode": "cool"
  }
}

// Query current temperature
{
  "command": "get_temperature",
  "arguments": {}
}
```

