A simple virtual device that models a TV’s basic controls.  
It exposes a set of actions that can be invoked programmatically or through a UI.

---

## Actions

| Action | Description | Parameters |
|--------|-------------|------------|
| **turnOn** | Turns the television on. | – |
| **turnOff** | Turns the television off. | – |
| **setChannel** | Sets the channel of the television. | `channel` (integer) |
| **setVolume** | Sets the volume level of the television. | `volume` (integer) |
| **changeInput** | Changes the input source of the television. | `inputSource` (string) |

> **Note:** All parameters are required for the actions that need them.

---

## Example Usage

```json
// Turn the TV on
{ "action": "turnOn" }

// Set channel to 5
{ "action": "setChannel", "input": { "channel": 5 } }

// Change volume to 20
{ "action": "setVolume", "input": { "volume": 20 } }

// Switch to HDMI 2
{ "action": "changeInput", "input": { "inputSource": "HDMI 2" } }

// Turn the TV off
