---

## Device ID

```
9db898c2-72af-47d4-8d19-2f2a2edb0dbe
```

---

## Supported Actions

| Action | Title | Description | Input |
|--------|-------|-------------|-------|
| `turn_on` | Turn On | Turns the speaker on. | None |
| `turn_off` | Turn Off | Turns the speaker off. | None |
| `set_volume` | Set Volume | Sets the speaker volume. | `{ "volume": <integer> }` |
| `play_music` | Play Music | Plays a specified song on the speaker. | `{ "song": "<string>" }` |
| `stop_music` | Stop Music | Stops any music currently playing. | None |

---

## Quick Start

```json
// Turn the speaker on
{
  "action": "turn_on"
}

// Set volume to 25
{
  "action": "set_volume",
  "input": { "volume": 25 }
}

// Play a song
{
  "action": "play_music",
  "input": { "song": "Imagine" }
}

// Stop the music
{
  "action": "stop_music"
}

// Turn the speaker off
{
  "action": "turn_off"
}
```

---

## Notes

- The `volume` value is an integer; the valid range is device‑specific (check the device documentation for limits).
- The `song` field expects the exact name or identifier of a song available to the speaker.
- All actions are idempotent where applicable (e.g., calling `turn_on` on an already‑on speaker has no adverse effect).

