el': 'Music Player', 'components': [{'capabilities': [{'id': 'music', 'commands': {'play': {'arguments': []}, 'stop': {'arguments': []}, 'setSource': {'arguments': [{'name': 'source', 'optional': False, 'schema_': {'type': 'string'}}]}, 'setGenre': {'arguments': [{'name': 'genre', 'optional': False, 'schema_': {'type': 'string'}}]}, 'setYearRange': {'arguments': [{'name': 'startYear', 'optional': False, 'schema_': {'type': 'integer'}}, {'name': 'endYear', 'optional': False, 'schema_': {'type': 'integer'}}]}, 'setDevice': {'arguments': [{'name': 'device', 'optional': False, 'schema_': {'type': 'string'}}]}}, 'version': 1, 'status': 'live'}], 'id': 'main', 'label': 'main', 'optional': False}], 'format': 'SmartThings', 'deviceId': '3d47aa9b-23d0-4bca-9168-9dc95b629253'}, 'natural': '# Music Player – SmartThings Device

A compact SmartThings‑compatible music player that can be controlled via a simple command set.  
The device is identified by the ID **3d47aa9b-23d0-4bca-9168-9dc95b629253** and is always live.

---

## Features

| Command | Description | Arguments |
|---------|-------------|-----------|
| `play` | Starts playback. | – |
| `stop` | Stops playback. | – |
| `setSource` | Selects a music source (e.g., “radio”, “bluetooth”, “USB”). | `source` (string) |
| `setGenre` | Filters tracks by genre (e.g., “rock”, “jazz”). | `genre` (string) |
| `setYearRange` | Filters tracks by release year range. | `startYear` (int), `endYear` (int) |
| `setDevice` | Chooses an external device to output audio (e.g., “speakers”, “headphones”). | `device` (string) |

All commands are available through the SmartThings API or via the SmartThings mobile app.

---

## Quick Start

```json
// Play music
{
  "command": "play"
}

// Set source to Bluetooth
{
  "command": "setSource",
  "arguments": {
    "source": "bluetooth"
  }
}

// Filter by genre
{
  "command": "setGenre",
  "arguments": {
    "genre": "jazz"
  }
}

// Set year range 1990‑2000
{
  "command": "setYearRange",
  "arguments": {
    "startYear": 1990,
    "endYear": 2000
  }
}

// Output to headphones
{
  "command": "setDevice",
  "arguments": {
    "device": "headphones"
  }
}
```

---

## Integration Notes

- The device follows the **SmartThings** format, so it can be added to any SmartThings‑compatible hub or app.
- No additional drivers are required; all commands are exposed via the standard SmartThings command interface.
- The device is **live** and ready for immediate use.

---

