e': 'integer'}}]}}, 'version': 1, 'status': 'live'}], 'id': 'main', 'label': 'main', 'optional': False}], 'format': 'SmartThings', 'deviceId': 'cc1de8c6-2d55-4ffb-82b7-016a8c81a7e9'}, 'natural': '# Living Room Speaker – SmartThings Device

**Device ID:** `cc1de8c6-2d55-4ffb-82b7-016a8c81a7e9`  
**Label:** *Living Room Speaker*  
**Component:** `main` (required)

---

## Overview

The Living Room Speaker is a SmartThings‑compatible media player that can stream audio from any URL and adjust its volume. It exposes a single `media_control` capability with three core commands:

| Command | Purpose | Arguments |
|---------|---------|-----------|
| `play` | Start streaming media | `media_url` (required, string) <br> `volume` (optional, integer) |
| `stop` | Stop playback | none |
| `set_volume` | Change the speaker’s volume | `volume` (required, integer) |

All commands are available via the SmartThings API, SmartThings Classic, or the SmartThings mobile app.

---

## Quick Start

### 1. Add the Device
- In the SmartThings mobile app or web interface, add a new device.
- Choose **“Custom Device”** and paste the JSON below (or use the SmartThings CLI to register it).

```json
{
  "name": "speaker",
  "label": "Living Room Speaker",
  "components": [
    {
      "id": "main",
      "label": "main",
      "optional": false,
      "capabilities": [
        {
          "id": "media_control",
          "version": 1,
          "status": "live",
          "commands": {
            "play": {
              "arguments": [
                { "name": "media_url", "optional": false, "schema_": { "type": "string" } },
                { "name": "volume",    "optional": true,  "schema_": { "type": "integer" } }
              ]
            },
            "stop": { "arguments": [] },
            "set_volume": {
              "arguments": [
                { "name": "volume", "optional": false, "schema_": { "type": "integer" } }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "format": "SmartThings",
  "deviceId": "cc1de8c6-2d55-4ffb-82b7-016a8c81a7e9"
}
```

> **Tip:** If you’re using the SmartThings CLI, run `st device register <path-to-json>`.

### 2. Control the Speaker

#### Play a Song

```bash
# Using SmartThings API
POST /api/smartapps/installations/<APP_ID>/devices/cc1de8c6-2d55-4ffb-82b7-016a8c81a7e9/commands
{
  "commands": [
    {
      "component": "main",
      "capability": "media_control",
      "command": "play",
      "arguments": {
        "media_url": "https://example.com/music/track.mp3",
        "volume": 30
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

#### Stop Playback

```bash
# Using SmartThings API
POST /api/smartapps/installations/<APP_ID>/devices/cc1de8c6-2d55-4ffb-82b7-016a8c81a7e9/commands
{
  "commands": [
    {
      "component": "main",
      "capability": "media_control",
      "command": "stop",
      "arguments": {}
    }
  ]
}
```

#### Change Volume

```bash
# Using SmartThings API
POST /api/smartapps/installations/<APP_ID>/devices/cc1de8c6-2d55-4ffb-82b7-016a8c81a7e9/commands
{
  "commands": [
    {
      "component": "main",
      "capability": "media_control",
      "command": "set_volume",
      "arguments": {
        "volume": 45
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

> **Volume Range:** 0 (mute) – 100 (max).  
> **media_url** must be a publicly accessible URL that streams audio in a supported format (MP3, AAC, etc.).

### 3. Automate with SmartThings Apps

Create a SmartApp that triggers the `play` command when a motion sensor detects movement, or set the volume based on the time of day. The device’s single component and straightforward commands make it easy to integrate into any routine.

---

## Troubleshooting

| Issue | Possible Fix |
|-------|--------------|
| Speaker does not respond | Verify the device ID and that the SmartThings hub can reach the speaker’s network. |
| Volume changes don’t stick | Ensure the `volume` argument is an integer between 0 and 100. |
| Media fails to play | Check that the `media_url` is reachable and the file format is supported. |

---

## Support

For questions, feature requests, or bug reports, please open an issue in the project’s GitHub repository or contact the maintainer at `support@example.com`.

