---

## Overview

This document describes the **TV** device and its available actions. The TV can be controlled programmatically through a set of defined actions, each with a clear title and description. The specification follows the W3C format for device descriptions.

---

## Actions

| Action | Title | Description | Input |
|--------|-------|-------------|-------|
| `turn_on` | Turn On | Turn on the TV | None |
| `turn_off` | Turn Off | Turn off the TV | None |
| `set_channel` | Set Channel | Set the TV to a specific channel | `{"channel": <integer>}` |

### set_channel Input Schema
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "channel": {
      "type": "integer"
    }
  },
  "required": ["channel"]
}
```

---

## Example Usage

```json
// Turn on the TV
{
  "action": "turn_on"
}

// Set the TV to channel 7
{
  "action": "set_channel",
  "input": {
    "channel": 7
  }
}

// Turn off the TV
{
  "action": "turn_off"
}
```

---

## Notes

- All actions are synchronous and return a success/failure status.
- The `set_channel` action requires an integer channel number; ensure the value is within the supported range for your TV model.

